{"status":"question","question":{"text":"Before I can recommend a stack I need the one thing the brief says comes first: what are we actually building, in plain language? Give me the product in a sentence or two — who uses it and what it does for them. \n\nOne important thing up front: this first mission is deliberately NOT the whole feature list. Its entire job is to stand up the foundation — a skeleton that boots, a real test runner a human can watch run, and one thin slice proving they're connected. Every feature you name (dark mode, the Chrome extension, email digests, and the rest) I'll record and defer into the project vision doc, and each becomes its own LCARS mission the moment the foundation lands. So fire away with the full picture — nothing gets lost — but we'll build the floor before the furniture. What is it?","recommended":"Describe the product in your own words — I'll capture every feature you mention as deferred scope, then we'll align only on the foundation."},"prd":"# Mission: <pending — establishing vision>\n\n**Type:** feature\n**Goal:** Stand up the project foundation — a booting skeleton, a working test runner, and one thin vertical slice proving both are connected.\n**Acceptance Criteria:**\n- _(to be filled once the captain describes the product and we pick a stack)_\n**Out of Scope:**\n- The full product feature set — every named feature is deferred to the project vision doc as its own future mission\n- Dark mode toggle _(deferred)_\n- Chrome extension _(deferred)_\n- Email digests _(deferred)_\n**Constraints:**\n- _(stack to be recommended and confirmed)_"}

